{"step_index":5649,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T19:44:39Z","thinking":"Encountering a \"no_match\" status from the comparison, a further check is necessary. If the classification of the item pair indicates \"review,\" then this discrepancy will be flagged for pharmacist review. Any \"reject\" classification requires additional handling, which I'll address later.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":"false","Description":"\"Update SYSTEM_PROMPT in coordinator.py to align with pharmacist rules\"","EndLine":"92","Instruction":"\"Refine prompt rules for strict brand OCR, zero strength tolerance, and form review\"","ReplacementContent":"\"SYSTEM_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are an expert clinical and Egyptian pharmaceutical matching assistant.\\nYou match requested drug names from pharmacy shortages with candidate items available in wholesale drug warehouses.\\n\\nCRITICAL PHARMACEUTICAL RULES:\\n1. STRICT BRAND IDENTITY (NO GENERICS / NO ALTERNATIVES):\\n   - You MUST match the EXACT SAME commercial trade brand name.\\n   - NEVER suggest or accept alternative brand names, different trade names, or generics (e.g. Panadol is NOT Cetal, Brufen is NOT Cataflam, Augmentin is NOT Curam, Ebastine is NOT Loratadine, Triactin is NOT Claritin, Sinopril is NOT Sinupret, Depozine is NOT Diosmin).\\n   - If the trade brand is a different commercial brand or generic substitute, YOU MUST RETURN \\\"status\\\": \\\"no_match\\\" (or omit it).\\n   - Allow common Arabic OCR scanning artifacts, dropped letters/syllables, phonetic variants, and Arabic/Persian letter substitutions of the SAME exact commercial brand (e.g. فيوسيدين/فيوسيدل where connected 'ين' is read as 'ل', ميبو/ميو where 'ب' is dropped, بروفين/برونفين, امبوفير/اميفير, ديباكين/ديبيكان, or dropped initial 'ا', dropped single letters or missing dots like 'ن' or 'ب', Persian/Urdu letters like پ for ب or ک for ك or گ for ك/ج, visually conf